Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.30,0:00:06.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Browser agents look reliable when we test whether they work once.\NAgentGauntlet tests whether they survive production.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:13.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Same task. Same agent. Four environments.\NReal Solari cloud browsers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.00,0:00:21.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Baseline passes in 7 steps. Then the session expires\Nmid-task — and the agent fails.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:30.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,This one passed. It also went from 7 steps to 19.\NA pass/fail benchmark records that as identical to baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:38.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,We never trust the agent saying it's done. The evaluator reads\Nthe benchmark site's server-side state, which the agent can't fake.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.00,0:00:45.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Every failure is classified from evidence —\Nthis one is an auth failure the agent never recovered from.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.00,0:00:52.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Bring your own agent. Your repository runs inside an isolated\NSolari Sandbox, with a scoped browser endpoint — never the account key.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.00,0:00:59.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Four runs is a demonstration, not a benchmark —\Nand the product shows the confidence interval to prove it.
